WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.672
Hi! Welcome to Opportunities.

00:02.672 --> 00:05.192
Opportunities is a new app
for the Edovo platform

00:05.192 --> 00:08.213
that helps you understand 
your potential release dates

00:08.213 --> 00:11.453
and the different types of release
you may be eligible for.

00:11.453 --> 00:13.394
With Opportunities, you can:

00:13.394 --> 00:17.034
View the release dates you currently
receive from the Legal Record Office or

00:17.034 --> 00:18.495
your Case Manager.

00:18.495 --> 00:22.556
Learn what different release types mean,
including the requirements and conditions

00:22.556 --> 00:24.136
in plain language.

00:24.136 --> 00:27.757
We also share this disclaimer to note
that this application is for general

00:27.757 --> 00:31.678
and supplemental purposes only.
It is not intended to be substituted

00:31.678 --> 00:34.639
for the official record
of this information.

00:34.639 --> 00:37.920
Now, we're in the portal.
This is what you'll see.

00:37.920 --> 00:41.981
The general structure is a homepage
that shows your release and review types,

00:41.981 --> 00:47.903
and an explainer page with information
about what the dates mean.

00:47.903 --> 00:51.104
The first thing you'll see is this
light gray banner at the top.

00:51.104 --> 00:54.545
This banner shows the date
the information was last changed.

00:54.545 --> 00:57.426
If you have any questions about
when the data will be updated,

00:57.426 --> 00:59.983
you should always refer to this banner.

00:59.983 --> 01:03.804
If we scroll, the next section shows
your important dates.

01:03.804 --> 01:07.665
These are all of the projected release dates
that the Legal Records Office has calculated

01:07.665 --> 01:09.385
for a resident's sentence.

01:09.385 --> 01:14.886
These dates are subject to change, based on
changes to Good Time and parole denial.

01:14.886 --> 01:17.406
We know sentence dates can be confusing.

01:17.406 --> 01:21.607
That's exactly why each date here
comes with a plain English summary,

01:21.607 --> 01:26.707
so you're not left guessing or relying
on secondhand information from the yard.

01:26.707 --> 01:29.688
You may see several different possible
release or review types,

01:29.688 --> 01:31.268
depending on your sentence.

01:31.268 --> 01:33.789
Not everybody will have all
of the possible dates.

01:33.789 --> 01:36.570
The app only shows the dates
that apply to you.

01:36.570 --> 01:40.971
You will see the sentence name, the date,
the amount of time from the date,

01:40.971 --> 01:43.923
and summary in plain English.

01:43.923 --> 01:48.765
If you scroll to the bottom of the page and
click on the Learn More About Dates button,

01:48.765 --> 01:51.446
you'll be taken to an explainer
page with information about

01:51.446 --> 01:54.167
what the review dates and release dates mean.

01:54.167 --> 01:59.110
Each link directly corresponds to a specific
explanation on the following:

01:59.110 --> 02:00.551
What do my dates mean?

02:00.551 --> 02:03.253
An explanation on how Good Time
can affect dates.

02:03.253 --> 02:06.136
An explanation of credits
that can shorten a sentence.

02:06.136 --> 02:09.398
An explanation of why some credits
don't impact dates.

02:09.398 --> 02:11.820
Guide on how Transitional Housing works.

02:11.820 --> 02:13.942
Information about the STEP Program.

02:13.942 --> 02:16.864
Instructions for what to do post-release.

02:16.864 --> 02:20.967
A "What happens if..." section to answer
common situational questions.

02:20.967 --> 02:23.589
Information on how dates are calculated.

02:23.589 --> 02:27.492
Information about the labels on the
Parole Board Review Date.

02:27.492 --> 02:31.015
An explanation for individuals serving
more than one sentence at a time,

02:31.015 --> 02:32.777
concurrent and consecutive.

02:32.777 --> 02:35.539
And a statement to submit a kite
to the Legal Records Office

02:35.539 --> 02:38.121
for additional sentence questions.

02:38.121 --> 02:42.425
As I mentioned, if you click on any of
these subheaders, you'll be taken directly

02:42.425 --> 02:45.443
to the section on this full page.

02:45.443 --> 02:49.967
This page is very robust and includes all
commonly asked questions you may have.

02:49.967 --> 02:52.649
If you would like to return to
the homepage, you'll scroll up and

02:52.649 --> 02:55.291
click on this "Back to Home" button.

02:55.291 --> 02:58.654
Ultimately, this app itself is
designed to be very simple.

02:58.654 --> 03:03.958
Just two pages: one that shows your release
and review dates in the demo video,

03:03.958 --> 03:08.419
and another containing descriptions
about those dates.

03:08.419 --> 03:10.401
A few final important notes.

03:10.401 --> 03:15.085 
A banner at the top of your tablet screen will
tell you when the data has been last updated.

03:15.085 --> 03:18.527
The app refreshes every day, but
you may not notice any changes

03:18.527 --> 03:21.230
unless your release date has
changed for some reason.

03:21.230 --> 03:24.012
For example, good time credit updates.

03:24.012 --> 03:26.414
This tool will only live on your tablet.

03:26.414 --> 03:29.877
It will only show your own information,
not others'.

03:29.877 --> 03:32.499
It will not show information
about your crime.

03:32.499 --> 03:37.553
The app pulls directly from Elite
and is not a separate calculation.

03:37.553 --> 03:39.822
Thank you for learning more about Opportunities.
